    "narrative": "Our primary offensive anchor today is **Bryce Harper**, who leads the board with an elite 75.38 score against G. Holmes. **Harper** benefits from a massive 17% SP skill boost and favorable order placement, making him the clear priority for production. Close behind is **Cal Raleigh** (79.31), whose power-hitting profile against the vulnerable Jacob Lopez (4.77 xERA) creates an ideal matchup scenario, provided he slots into the heart of the order as expected. We are also leaning heavily into **Lawrence Butler** (68.17); while the matchup against Bryce Miller is tough, **Butler** benefits from a 13% dynamic platoon edge and a projected #3 slot, maintaining his status as a high-upside play. **Justin Crawford** also remains essential for our rotation; despite a lower base, his elite speed profile\u2014critical for our category-specific strategy\u2014combined with the favorable matchup against G. Holmes keeps his efficiency score comfortably strong at 62.71.\n\nThe roster optimization process forced a difficult cut between **Daulton Varsho** (59.91) and **Dylan Beavers** (49.13). While **Beavers** provides elite speed and is a regular contributor to our SB goals, the optimizer prioritized **Varsho** today due to a significant 14% platoon advantage and a superior overall projected efficiency against F. Peralta. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (57.74); despite his star pedigree, the matchup against an elite arm like Joe Ryan (3.36 xERA) drags his raw projection down. Additionally, we are monitoring the status of **Zack Gelof** and **Cal Raleigh**, as both are currently reliant on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions; if these projected slots shift downward, their efficiency scores will need to be re-evaluated to prevent unnecessary depletion of our daily game caps.",
